> 30 Wizard of Yendor (only gives intrisic teleportation, human)

Why do you say that it only gives intrinsic telep?  I don't see anything in 
the eat.c code to verify this, and I know I've received intrinsic telep.
control from him, also.  I think you should be able to get any of the
intrinsics he has to offer (tport, tport control, fire res, poison res)
I think he is useful to eat especially in the case of teleport control,
which is a hard intrinsic to get since so few monsters offer it.  If you
unluckily manage to get down to him without getting tport control from a
tengu, he's your best bet, since he's 30th level, and will automatically
guarantee getting the rare intrinsic (and also aggravate monster, if you're 
human).

> 1  barbarian (human)
> 1  healer (human)
> 6  wraith (cannot convey intrinsics)

The strategy I've found that works well with respect to poison and poison res
is to play it extremely safe on the early levels and don't touch any food
that's poisonous, while eating all the cave spiders and such that I can...
Once I get to the 4th or 5th level, I start looking for a unicorn to get a
horn from (and eat, too).  Once you get a unicorn horn, the attribute loss
isn't so frightening, since you can regain the lost points by #applying the
horn a bunch of times.  This gives you a little more leeway in what you can
eat, so you don't need to be quite so careful all the time.

